  {
    "episode_id": 89163,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Oh, totally. Well, first of all, you had to sort of pick the sport wrestling because I'm five, seven and a half on a good day. You know, even though I wanted to play middle linebacker, like I always tell people, like a lot of kids, when I was in grade school, I knew what I was going to do. I was going to play middle linebacker for the Pittsburgh Steelers because you and I grew up in the 70s. And it was the Raiders and the Steelers and the Cowboys. And I love the Steelers, me and Joe Green and all about my favorite guy. was Jack Lambert, but you've been around me, you know, the good Lord had other designs. So I had to wrestle, and that was something our family did, and our high school was a school that was pretty good for being a country school, but sort of the sport at our school. And my dad just had a huge impact on me and got us into wrestling, and it worked out well for our family. But yeah, there's something about it, and you've done it as well. I think people in all kinds of endeavors look at it this way. In sports, you learn to set the goal. You learn to work hard. And hopefully, if you work hard, good things happen. And you're actually able to reach the goal you've set. And it worked out pretty good for our family in wrestling. So yeah, it has an impact, I think, on everything you do.",
