    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Well, when you, a great question, when you go from the minority to the majority, you better know what you're going to do. And you better have worked on it as a team so that when you're in the majority, you're ready to actually do what you told the voters you were going to do, if in fact they put you in power and give you control of the government. I don't think we were ready, frankly, when we took the majority back in 10 in that election to really come in and focus in a and a really focused manner on dealing with the spending problem. If you remember, then it was the Tea Party issue or the else. And I think the same thing applied in 2017 when it came to Obamacare. So one of the things I think that we're hopefully going to be able to take back the majority and I believe Leader McCarthy is doing frankly much better. than the previous Republican leaders is he's keeping the team united and I'm hopeful that if in fact the American people put us back in charge we're going to come in and pass the things we need to pass Joe Biden won't sign him but we'll show the American people what we're for and then during the appropriations process we're going to we're going to fight from one or two key policies to get on those appropriation bills And I feel like we got a much better chance of getting something positive done, even with Joe Biden still in the White House. And I think that's a lot to do with Kevin's leadership. You know, no one kept us together over the last two years and it's obviously easier in the minority, but The convention, go back to impeachment. The convention of wisdom was during the first impeachment, every Democrat was going to vote to impeach President Trump and some Republicans were going to join him. When in fact, when we got done with that whole debate and that whole process, every Republican in the House voted against it, some Democrats joined us and won even switched parties. So that's a testament to Kevin and the leadership in our whole team working together as a team, and we're going to have to do that, like I said, if the American people put us back in charge.",
