    "turn_text": "Are you mentioning Kevin? Of course, that's Kevin McCarthy. I want to ask you a personality question. You were at one point the head of the RSC, which is the Republican Study Committee, a large, large group. And it's hard to become the head of that. And you were elected that. And I don't want to say that's leadership, but that is certainly more, I think, mainstream. And then you started something called the Freedom Caucus, which was a smaller group. I think it's probably fair to say more ideologically conservative, but if I'm wrong, you tell me that. But even when you were with the Freedom Caucus, it struck me that you always had a line of communication. You just mentioned Kevin McCarthy. Yeah. Even with the previous speakers with Paul and John, even if you disagreed with them, it always seemed to me as an outsider that you had a lane or line of communication with them. So how did you pull that off? RSC starting the Freedom",
