  {
    "episode_id": 89163,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "Well, I always try never to make a personal never never criticized, you know, speaker Boehner or speaker Ryan in the press. I just don't think that's way should should operate. And the reason though we created the freedom caucus is real simple. It's our mission statement. We talk about. You know, this town has forgotten the American family, American people. And our job is to remember the moms and dads, the families, the taxpayers across this country who feel like this town has completely abandoned them, completely forgotten them. When we get here, I mean, I wrote a book on this. Do what you said you would do. So our job is to come here and actually do what they elected us to do. It's not easy. I mean, you got 200 and some members, if you're in the majority, you got to kind of corral them and get them all moving in one direction. That ain't easy. And so I understand that the difficult task that both Speaker Boehner and Speaker Ryan had. But we tried to communicate with him. And I think we did a pretty good job of trying to reach out to him. Didn't always agree. There were times we had to push back in a big way. But I will tell you this I think it's been much better with with leader McCarthy and again it's easier in the minority I get that but I still think leader McCarthy has done a much better job of embracing the entire conference. And and maybe part of that's trades because And you know, when you were here was maybe not, well, it certainly wasn't as bad as is now, but the difference today is today's whatever differences may exist in the Republican Party between the more conservative members of the Republican Conference and maybe those who are more moderate. those pale in comparison to the differences between Republicans today and the radical left that controls the Democrat Party. Because there, you think about what they, there was one week last year trade. Think about this, one week and one week's time, the week started off with congresswoman, congresswoman, to leave saying we should get rid of police, not just defund him, get rid of police. The week started off with that, the weekend, and if you remember this week last spring, where the trial judge in Minneapolis admonished vaccine waters for the ridiculous things she said while the jury was deliberating and in between those two events you had the Democrats pass legislation to make DC estate and introduce legislation to pack the court. Those four things happen in a five-day time frame and like That's craziness. So that's what I think we now understand why it's important Republicans stick together to try to do what we told the American people were going to do, do what the country needs done. And like I said, I think Kevin's done just a tremendous job in that compared to previous leaders.",
