    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "If it all works out that way, Lord willing. Number one is two million illegal immigrants have crossed our border in one year's time. I mean just that's that's that's that's in that's deliberate that's intentional. We have to focus on that issue. Try to pass legislation that will that will help stop that. I don't know the game that Joe Biden will ever sign it because I think as I said when when last spring. March was the highest month on record for illegal crossings until April and then April was the highest month until May and then May till June and then June was the highest month until July and it just kept going up and it's basically stayed about that high level stripped it down a little bit, which tells you this has to be deliberate. So that issue is number one, has to be, and we have the Judiciary Committee has primary jurisdiction over that particular issue. Second, of course, is what's happened at the Justice Department, the weaponization of the Justice Department. And in particular, you can see this how it's played out with the whole school boards issue and the memorandum that the Attorney General issued just five days after the school board association sent a letter to the Biden administration. And we now know that it didn't start with that letter. The letter was the pretext to do what they wanted to do because there was communications prior to the letter ever being sent by the National School Board Association, communications between the Biden administration and the School Board Association. Basically, it was the template they always use. Give us the pretext to do what we want to do, which is go after our political enemies. It was the dossier was the pretext to go do what they want to do to spy on Trump's campaign. Same here in this situation. So that school board issue is critically important because it addresses a fundamental issue. just like the border. Fundamental issue, you got to have a border if you're going to be a nation. Fundamental issue is do moms and dads know what's best for their kids or does government? And you and I both understand it's moms and dads. Unfortunately, a lot of people in today's lab to control the Democrat Party actually believe it's government. So that to me, those two are the two most important And then there's just the broader concerns about the Justice Department, the FBI, the Hunter Biden issue. And some of those decisions are going to have to be made as a conference. But I think it's those are the priorities. And then finally, the last thing I mentioned is big tech. Now, this will mostly come out of energy and commerce, but the Section 230 changes need to happen. The concern we have with how big tech and big media are coming after conservatives and censoring conservatives like Trey Gowdy and the Babylon B and others. That's a huge issue. We'll have to focus on as well.",
