    "turn_text": "All right. When I travel the country, your name comes up quite often in photo lines. Other people ask me what's Jim Jordan like and I always start with his work ethic. And then I always say two things. The thing that I always liked about Jim is he would poke you in the chest, but he would never push you in the back. If he has a problem with you, he will come eyeball to eyeball. You don't have to worry about your back. You may get punched in the jaw, but you're not going to get punched in the back. And the other thing I tell him is he's really not afraid of anything. And so that leads me to this. People",
