  {
    "episode_id": 89163,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Well, what we tried to let the president know was we didn't think the bill that we'd introduced was consistent with what we told the voters were going to do. And I had this conversation with the president in person. Mark Minow's and I both did. And yeah, there was a time where we disagreed on that. But I think over the longer haul, the president learned that, oh, They were actually, they were on the right page. The bill wasn't what we told the voters were going to do. We got another bill that we passed out of the house. And unfortunately, John McCain, Senator McCain, gave it the thumbs down and we wound up not getting it done. So that was tough. I mean, I was one of the disappointments I had in that first two years when we were all in the majority and President Trump was in the White House. What I will say about President Trump that I think so many So many people, particularly them in this town, don't see us. He is a good man. He genuinely loves this. I've gotten to know him over there. I know you have his welts, right? I've gotten to know him. I speak to him often. I know he loves the country. He loves our military, loves our veterans, loves our law enforcement personnel, loves hardworking people who make the country special, who work hard every day, truly is fighting for America. And he got more done. in his first term in four years with everyone in this town against him. I mean, every Democrat was against him, everyone in the mainstream press was against him, a bunch of Republicans were against him, and certainly the bureaucracy, which is maybe the swamp that was against him. And in spite of that, got done what he said he would do more than any president in our lifetime. and take so much abuse. But I like, but yeah, early on, we had a disagreement on the health care bill. And I'll be honest with you, Trey. I thought the way Paul Ryan went about trying to overturn Obamacare was just completely wrong. And we told Paul that. And we told the White House, we don't think this is not what we said we would do. This bill doesn't have the votes. And it's not going to pass. And the process, the three bucket approaches, the craziest approach ever. And we learned the hard way that Freedom Caucus guys who opposed it, we were right in the long run. But as I said, it was unfortunate that Senator McCain took a different position there at the final, and the final piece, the final step. But as far as President Trump goes, man, I wanted to run again, Trey, and I think he's going to, and I think he's going to win.",
