  {
    "episode_id": 89163,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Oh, they're just a lot less fair. I mean, they're not even Everything you see from the mainstream press is almost always built on something false. It's misleading. It's sometimes just an outright lie. And they're just so much more gotchas, so much more out to get. I remember a conversation and it's funny to bring this up. I've shared this with some folks before, but a conversation I had with President Trump a few years ago is back during the whole Mueller stuff. And he had called me and I was actually in the cap of my step in this room and I'm walking around. Listen to the president we're talking and I'm just pacing around this table in some some room there in the Capitol and We were talking about McCabe and struck and pay all that stuff when it was all going on But at some point during the conversation I don't even know why it came up But I said to the I said the president said mr. President I know what I get I know how CNN and New York Times and MSNBC, they know how they lie about me and the things they say and all the book. I said, I know what I get. I know how bad that is, but you get it a thousand times worse and you get it every second of every stinking day. And there was a little pause. And then the president goes, well, Jim, what are you going to do? Go over in the corner, get in the fetal position, start sucking your thumb. He goes, we got to fight back. And I said, I agree, Mr. President, let's keep fighting. But that's the atmosphere I think the press has created because they're always out to get conservatives. And now it's gotten to, and the best examples, and it's obviously been in the news recently, the best example is the 100 Biden situation where you had big tech, big media, and the Democrats all collude to keep an important story from the American people just days before the most important election we have in our country, a presidential election. And it was all based on garbage. The laptop, as I said last week, the laptop was real, the eyewitness was real, and the documents, the emails were all real. The only thing fake a year and a half ago was the news, because they said it was disinformation. And you also had not just, you had big tech, big media, Democrats, and former Intel. People in the intelligence community all collude to say this was not a truth. I mean, so that's the problem with today's press.",
