    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89163.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 55,
    "turn_text": "They're different. But I tell golf is so frustrating and so hard. And you're good at it. I'm not. But I love the game. You know what I love about it? I love when I play with someone about my skill set, which is fairly bad. But if it's competitive, if it's coming down to the 18th hole, I like to play match play. Oh, that to me is the best because that is just like a big match last last minute of the match. You got to take it. It's the same dynamic and a golf is tough because it's the mental the something someone says something. You're backswing. You screw it up. You don't stop. You don't read so many things. Some one day you're putting well, you know this stuff. So But I love the game and the challenge of it. And I frankly, I like watching it. I've watched too much of it. Masters is coming up. I'll watch as much of that as my schedule will allow. But I've seen you play. I've seen you hit it. You can play. You were kind enough to come to our outing. First, Die Build course in the country. The Die Families from Urbana, Ohio. And we've done an outing there now like 20 some years in a row. You came about 10 years ago, did a great job.",
